<h1>Data Analytics for <a href="https://www.comics.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GCD</a></h1>

<h2>Explore GCD data in your browser</h2>
<div>
  <p>The <strong><a href="/explore/">Explore</a></strong> page lets you run SQL directly against the latest GCD snapshot
  without installing anything. Queries run entirely in your browser via
  <a href="https://duckdb.org/docs/api/wasm/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DuckDB WASM</a> —
  only the Parquet columns your query touches are downloaded.</p>
</div>

<h2>Redash dashboards</h2>
<div>
  <p>The <a href="https://github.com/youknowjack/gcd-etl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gcd-etl project</a>
  builds a denormalized Parquet snapshot for each GCD data dump using a Python/pyarrow pipeline. A self-hosted
  <a href="https://github.com/getredash/redash/blob/master/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Redash</a>
  instance backed by <a href="https://duckdb.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DuckDB</a> provides a
  front-end for authoring queries and dashboards.</p>
  <p>To get a sense of the types of analysis possible with this dataset, check out <a href="/redash-samples/">these
  sample queries</a>.</p>
  <p>You can learn more about the dataset and see the schema on the <a href="/about-redash/">about page</a>.</p>
</div>

<h2>Imhotep / IQL (historical)</h2>
<div>
  <p>The gcd-etl project previously produced a dataset in the Flamdex format used by
  <a href="https://github.com/indeedeng/imhotep" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Imhotep</a>, an OSS project
  from Indeed. You can browse the <a href="/imhotep-samples/">Imhotep sample queries</a> in the SQL-like
  Imhotep Query Language (IQL) for historical interest.</p>
</div>
<p><i>Note that there is no longer an active Imhotep cluster serving this data.</i></p>
